# CLAUDE.md and Cursor rules stay in sync

`.cursor/rules/*.mdc` and root `CLAUDE.md` are the **same project conventions** on two surfaces (Cursor vs Claude Code / Rider).

- After changing any file in `.cursor/rules/`, update `CLAUDE.md` in the **same session**.
- After changing `CLAUDE.md` conventions, update the matching `.mdc` (or add one) in the **same session**.
- Cursor files keep YAML frontmatter; `CLAUDE.md` is one markdown file without frontmatter.
- Do not let them drift. Do not maintain a third copy (no extra MEMORY.md).
- Local clone paths stay labeled **AI only**. Never copy those paths into `Documentation/`, `Brief/`, `TimeTracking/`, or `Solution/`.
